2. Create your own scenario that illustrates differences-in-differences. Describe the story behind the data and show whether there is a nonzero treatment effect.

A scenario that illustrates differences in differences would be testing to see how much fertilizer helps plants grow by having a control group that you just water, and then having a treatment group that you water and add fertilizer to. For these two groups, you would ensure that the plants have similar growing conditions like temperature, sun exposure, and water amount so the only difference between the two groups would be whether or not they have been given fertilizer. Due to the shared condition on water amount, you could subtract the benefit of water amount from the treatment groups benefit to get the benefit of having the fertilizer.

