One issue I encountered with this method is the x difference and/or y difference could be 0 or nan due to not having any values for one of the groups in a bin. This would lead to the calculated effect turning into NaN. To mitigate this issue, I added a check that will only calculate the effect if the x difference is not 0 or nan and the y difference is not nan. I otherwise did not encounter any other issues when writing this code. 

